== Inference
These are the Coordinator's readings and design choices; none is a measurement.

- *Classification:* #s("stopped_infrastructure") under AGENTS.md core rule 5 and DEC-20261106-475620 #s("dev1_decision_v2.outcomes.stopped_or_infrastructure"). It is not a KAT outcome and says nothing about the kernel's m = 3 large-q path, nothing about B1 except that DEV-1 has not run, and nothing about any prediction. The two helper-item passes are not a partial DEV-1 result (they precede the cell by design), and the projection-phase sub-base rates do not substitute for the full-pass rate SC-3 needs.
- *CG-1 (card gap, owned by the Coordinator):* the 96fee7 card set a 41,400 s watchdog but named no launch mechanism, and nothing recorded that a harness background task cannot outlive 7,200,000 ms. A card that cannot be honoured as written is the Coordinator's defect first; the executor's report calls the launch an executor error, and both readings are kept. SF-96fee7-1 is accepted as written.
- *Checkpointability:* at the bound bytes the cell is atomic. The cell item makes one call to #s("counters.arm_c_cell"), which makes one kernel call, one C call that enumerates every depth-3 multiset of the base and returns only at the end, with no intermediate state, range or resumable seed. Prefix sub-bases are cumulative, not partitioning, and any other split tests a different kernel path. A container restart therefore costs the whole attempt; a restartable or parallel cell needs a change to kernel.c or the bound test file (OQ-1 option C), which this act does not open.
- *Launcher design LD-1 to LD-12* (authoritative text: ledger/handoffs/TASK-20261107-bc7a76.yaml). LD-1 bytes re-verified per attempt, before-record written before the projection. LD-2 exactly the 96fee7 DX-2 argv, scratch paths only. LD-3 a fresh projection per attempt, at most 1,200 s, go only at or below 39,600 s, otherwise #s("stopped_projection") with no retry. LD-4 a recorded supervisor script that writes state.json, wraps the cell in a coreutils timeout at 41,400 s, writes a heartbeat every 600 s with the cell's VmHWM, writes exit.json at child exit, traps TERM, INT and HUP, and never restarts the cell. LD-5 launch by setsid nohup from one short foreground command, never a harness background task, recording pid, start time, pgid, boot\_id, PID 1 start time and uptime. LD-6 RESUME filled and pushed before every launch and at every terminal classification. LD-7 state directory outside the repository; re-attach from RESUME.md alone by single read-only check-ins about every 60 minutes, no sleep loop. LD-8 mechanical classification C1 to C8 (Figure 2, right). LD-9 retries only after C5, up to maximum\_attempts (2). LD-10 seven artifacts and cumulative DEV-1 wall accounting, attempt 1 included. LD-11 idle host. LD-12 zero runs, no KAT values in messages, never Bedrock.
- *Retry rule:* a container restart is #s("stopped_infrastructure (container_restart)") for that attempt and the only retriable cause; watchdog, signalled, unexplained\_kill, crash, OOM and #s("stopped_projection") go back to a fresh act without retry. A completed cell is never re-run for a different answer. If every allowed attempt is lost to restarts, the outcome is #s("stopped_infrastructure_retries_exhausted").
- *Allowance reading:* the owner's grant is not presumed to cover a re-run. Attempt 1 used about 2.5 h of the 43,200 s budget and the rest cannot hold the cell; one fresh attempt brings DEV-1 to about 13-14.3 h, two to about 26 h; docs/research-budget-policy.md is applied by analogy; and ENV-2 is a fact the owner did not have. Hence OQ-1. Everything else proceeds without the answer.
- *Review first (R-P1 to R-P5):* the 10.5 h cell must run on the final launcher bytes, so the re-review goes first and a late launcher fix cannot void a finished cell; DEV-1 now waits on the owner; RR-1 to RR-4 and RR-6 to RR-8 do not read the cell output; the cell needs an idle host (max\_concurrent 1); RR-9 red-teams the launcher design before compute depends on it. 941825 RR-5 moves verbatim to a DEV-1 verification task written by the releasing act.
- *B8 split:* *B8-H* clears when 971edf archives a 7db1de report finding every hardening must-fix closed (N-5 item 5, NF-1 to NF-7, the receipt clash; M6, M5 and M3 killed by the reviewer's own runs; plan byte-identical) and no new blocking finding. *B8-D* clears when the DEV-1 verification confirms, on the eebc5b commit, outcome passed, the cell run in full on the 5d5a607d bytes, and the reviewer's own kernel-free membership counts agreeing on at least 10 logged targets. *B8* clears when both have. The decisive evidence is unchanged, only divided between two reports. SC-4 (allow-list digest by the dfd0ed method, the other as an alias) and SC-5 (the approval names the eebc5b, 971edf and verification commits; SC-3 uses the full-pass rate, never projection-phase rates) are added to the approval act.

*OQ-1*, quoted in full (#s("owner_questions[OQ-1].text; status open") in this decision):
