Owner answer relayed after this decision: (A); recorded by a later act.

== Limitation
- *Environment facts as reported and unverified:* ENV-1 to ENV-5 are operational observations of the host reported by the top-level session; the act did not verify them. Commits, the PR number, digests and the environment facts are as the session and the committed receipts report; the act ran no tool and computed no hash.
- *Restart rate unknown:* the container restart rate is not recorded, so no probability that an attempt finishes is stated. bc7a76 records uptime and restart signals at every launch and check-in. Restart detection relies on boot\_id, PID 1 start time and uptime; a restart that changes none of them would be classified unexplained\_kill and not retried (the conservative direction; RR-9 may sharpen it).
- *Session-only independence:* 7db1de is independent of the producers between sessions only, not between models (resolved model claude-opus-5-5, model\_verified false). This is not a rule-12 round.
- *KAT-field scope:* DEV-1 checks a code path on a KAT field (F\_{10007^2}, m = 3), not a contract configuration. Toy tier throughout; KN-OPEN-62c870 CS-D2 and CS-R7 bind every later citation. L-2 (N-6) stands as in DEC-20261106-843cf7; receipts and the code\_tree block are not cryptographically authenticated.
- *This report re-ran nothing:* figure-data.json copies values by key; its few sums and time differences (the projection offsets, the 8,820 s attempt-1 task wall, the cumulative ends and the grant band in seconds) are written out there with their derivation, and figures.py derives only layout and labels.

